CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--dfcc main --apply-loop-contracts
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
\[main\.assigns\.\d+\] line \d+ Check that t is assignable: FAILURE
--
--
Checks that a variable declared before a loop without an initializer is not
classified as a loop local when an explicit assigns clause is used, so that
writing to t (which is missing from the assigns clause) is flagged.
See GitHub issue #9175.
